  "sourceNotes": "Sarde in saor is one of the oldest dishes of the Venetian lagoon, eaten by fishermen and sailors for centuries. The sweet and sour marinade preserved the sardines on long sea voyages. It is traditionally eaten during the Feast of the Redeemer in July.",
