  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "glossaryTooltip",
            "attrs": {
              "termSlug": "saor"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " in this dish is the sweet and sour onion mixture that you layer over the fried sardines and leave to work overnight. The process of "
          },
          {
            "type": "glossaryTooltip",
            "attrs": {
              "termSlug": "marinating"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for 24 hours or more softens the fish, mellows the vinegar, and lets the raisins and pine nuts perfume the whole dish. This recipe serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Do not rush this dish. Made and eaten the same day it is sharp and flat. After 48 hours it becomes something completely different."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
